!! $:/tags/Stylesheet

`styles.tid` is tagged `$:/tags/Stylesheet`. TiddlyWiki collects all tiddlers with this tag at startup and injects their text content as `<style>` elements in the page `<head>`. The CSS is wikified first, which is what allows `<<colour ...>>` macro expansion.

!! <<colour>> macro

TiddlyWiki's palette system provides the `<<colour name>>` macro, which resolves to a CSS color value from the active palette tiddler (e.g., `$:/palettes/Vanilla`). The theme stylesheet uses this for borders, backgrounds, and text colors to ensure visual consistency with the user's chosen palette.

Key palette entries used:

|!Macro |!Typical value |!Usage in theme |
|`<<colour tiddler-border>>` |`#dbdbdb` |Tab borders, panel borders |
|`<<colour page-background>>` |`#f4f4f4` |Tab bar background |
|`<<colour muted-foreground>>` |`#999` |Inactive tabs, muted text |
|`<<colour foreground>>` |`#333` |Active tab text |
|`<<colour background>>` |`#fff` |Panel backgrounds |
|`<<colour primary>>` |`#5778d8` |Active tab border, link buttons |
|`<<colour alert-highlight>>` |`#ffe476` |Warning notices |

!! $transclude with $fill

The callout and notice templates use `\parameters` to declare their attributes, and `<$slot $name="body"/>` to insert consumer-provided content. Consumers use `<$transclude $tiddler="...">` with `<$fill $name="body">` to inject content. This creates a transclusion boundary that enables slot/fill matching.

!! Stylesheet loading order

TiddlyWiki loads stylesheet tiddlers in title-alphabetical order. The theme's `styles.tid` has title `$:/plugins/rimir/theme/styles`, which sorts after TW core styles. Plugin-specific styles in other rimir plugins sort after theme due to their longer title paths, so they can safely override theme classes with equal specificity.

